WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.640
Speaker 1: Bloomberg first reported, and Axios was&nbsp;
able to independently confirmed that President Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:11.280
Biden in his new White House budget is going to be&nbsp;
proposing a number of new taxes. I'm going to tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.240
you what they are, and then we will discuss&nbsp;
whether they are likely to become a reality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:25.500
Axios writes. The new budget request to Congress,&nbsp;
set to be released Thursday includes a 25% minimum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:36.060
tax on the richest 0.01% of Americans. This is&nbsp;
a billionaire tax. It would also increase the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:44.880
top tax rate for those Americans making $400,000&nbsp;
a year, up to 39.6% from 37%. That was the rate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:51.300
prior to Trump's 27 tax bill. 2017 tax bill. It&nbsp;
would go back to that prior rate. It would raise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:57.360
income levies on corporations and billionaires,&nbsp;
and it would set the corporate tax rate at 28%,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:05.100
still below the 35% rate that was in place prior&nbsp;
to Trump's 2017 tax law. That is not the only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:10.980
thing that Joe Biden plans to do. He also plans&nbsp;
an increased Medicare tax. Remember when we talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:16.740
about Social Security and Medicare? Sometimes&nbsp;
people forget about the Medicare piece. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:25.260
Joe Biden wants to do is increase the Medicare&nbsp;
tax rate from 3.8 to 5% on income, exceeding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:34.140
$400,000 per year, and it would apply to both&nbsp;
salaries as well as capital gains. It would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:41.580
likely increase tax revenues by over $117 billion&nbsp;
over ten years, so about 11.7 billion a year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:48.240
according to prior estimates from last month by&nbsp;
the Tax Policy Center. So a couple of different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:54.840
things. Is Joe Biden sticking to his promise&nbsp;
not to increase taxes on people making under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:00.420
$400,000 a year by all reasonable assessments of&nbsp;
these proposals? The answer is yes. Joe Biden is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:07.920
not raising taxes on anyone making under 400 k.&nbsp;
Secondly, is this likely to pass? And the answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:13.740
is no. I made this analysis when Donald Trump&nbsp;
would release his budgets and it is the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:19.680
analysis when Joe Biden releases his budget.&nbsp;
White House budgets are political documents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.720
Political documents. You have to get this through&nbsp;
the House of Representatives, currently controlled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:30.300
by Republicans in order to make it a reality. And&nbsp;
so this is a sort of wish list. This is what you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:36.480
could say Joe Biden would do if he could wave a&nbsp;
magic wand. And to be totally honest. Sometimes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.640
presidents include things in White House budgets&nbsp;
that they wouldn't actually do if they had full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:47.760
power to do it. They include it in the budget&nbsp;
as a signal, a virtue signal. We have to admit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:53.100
knowing that it's not going to pass. Which&nbsp;
category are these proposals under? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:57.780
we don't know because we know that it is a White&nbsp;
House budget, which is a political document. So it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:04.020
will be interesting to see, however, are there&nbsp;
negotiations to be had where Republicans who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:09.480
control the House would be willing to come to&nbsp;
the table on some of these proposals from Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:15.660
Biden in exchange for what? Well, we don't&nbsp;
really know. In exchange for what? We will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:22.200
be watching it. But so far, these proposals,&nbsp;
as unlikely as they are to become the law, are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:29.580
keeping Joe Biden adhered to the promise he made&nbsp;
about Americans making under $400,000 per year.

